OMT (Open Media Transport)
--------------------------
The OMT adapter uses MikanseiLaboratory/openmediatransport-rs and vmx-rs,
pure-Rust independent community implementations licensed under MIT. It does
not link or fall back to libomt.

Blackmagic DeckLink / Desktop Video
-----------------------------------
DeckLink, Desktop Video, and Blackmagic Design are trademarks of Blackmagic
Design Pty. Ltd. The Blackmagic Desktop Video SDK is proprietary. Default
builds do not compile or link SDK code and expose no simulated DeckLink
backend.

The explicit `decklink-sdk` feature compiles eiviz's MIT-licensed C ABI shim
against an operator-installed Desktop Video SDK 16 and the official platform
dispatch/interface source found below `DECKLINK_SDK_DIR`. SDK headers, source,
libraries, drivers, examples, documentation, and tools are not vendored,
downloaded, generated, or redistributed by this repository.

Building, testing, or distributing DeckLink support requires accepting and
complying with the current Blackmagic Design Desktop Video SDK license and any
driver/runtime redistribution restrictions. Distributors must obtain the SDK
directly from Blackmagic Design, review the license included with that exact
SDK release, preserve required notices, and verify whether any runtime files
may be shipped. That license, not this notice, is authoritative. See
https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/developer/product/capture-and-playback.

ASIO
----
ASIO is a trademark and technology of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH.
The MIT/Apache-2.0 CPAL and asio-sys crates expose the optional ASIO host, but
the Steinberg ASIO SDK remains separately licensed. An ASIO adapter is not
