an operator-installed, license-reviewed SDK selected with `CPAL_ASIO_DIR`;
shipping ASIO support requires compliance with Steinberg's current terms.
ASIO-enabled artifacts must remain a separately reviewed distribution profile.

CPAL
----
The optional audio adapter uses CPAL 0.18.2 (Apache-2.0) and rtrb 0.4.0
(MIT OR Apache-2.0). CPAL links platform audio APIs only in explicit audio
feature profiles. Native PipeWire builds additionally link PipeWire libraries
under their applicable licenses; default builds compile no CPAL system backend.

H.264 / AVC
-----------
The in-tree Baseline I_PCM encoder is compiled for tests only and is not
selectable as a recording or network profile. Production software encode and
decode dynamically load an end-user-installed Cisco OpenH264 2.6.0 binary from
an explicit path after checking its SHA-256 against `openh264-sys2`'s Cisco
binary allow-list and checking the runtime version. It must not be bundled and
must display "OpenH264 Video Codec provided by Cisco Systems, Inc." with
Cisco's binary license. Compiling OpenH264 source does not receive Cisco's
binary patent coverage and is not the selected profile. Product distributions
that encode or decode AVC may still require additional patent review.

The AAC-LC encode and file-decode adapters dynamically load an explicitly
selected FDK AAC shared library through the upstream raw-access-unit C ABIs.
No FDK binary or source is included in this repository. FDK AAC's bespoke
upstream license grants no patent rights; operators and distributors must
review that exact binary, its provenance, and all applicable patent/license
obligations before enabling either profile. Missing or rejected FDK binaries
are hard errors; AAC is not dropped, and PCM/test bytes or another codec are
never used as substitutes.

RTMP / SRT
----------
The distribution transport uses `rml_rtmp` 0.8.0 (MIT) and `srt-tokio` 0.4.4
(Apache-2.0). Both are pure Rust. Local protocol tests do not establish
interoperability certification; real-server and loss testing remains required.
The SRT implementation is independent from Haivision's MPL-2.0 reference
library and does not link `libsrt`.

gpu-video
---------
The optional `eiviz-codec-gpu-video` crate may depend on gpu-video 0.4.x
(MIT) behind a feature flag. It is not compiled into the default GUI path
so wgpu 24 (egui) and wgpu 29 (gpu-video) cannot collide.

GStreamer / FFmpeg
------------------
Neither GStreamer nor FFmpeg is a dependency. If a future distribution enables
those adapters, their LGPL/GPL obligations and each selected plugin's license
apply to that build and must be documented in the shipping SBOM. FDK AAC is
not bundled: its upstream bespoke license grants no patent rights.
